    "durationMs": 343336,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What I built** (Rails 8.0.2 API-only, PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`):\n- `POST /links` — validates absolute http/https URLs with a host, optional custom code (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`), generates unique 8-char codes otherwise; 201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}` (URL returned unchanged), 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 on invalid/missing url, invalid code, or malformed JSON\n- `GET /links/{code}` — 200 with link JSON, 404 JSON for unknown codes\n- `GET /r/{code}` — 302 with `Location` set to the stored URL and an atomic one-time click increment, 404 JSON for unknown codes\n- `GET /links` — `{items: [...], total: n}` in ascending creation order\n- Catch-all route so any unmatched path/method also returns 404 JSON\n\n**Environment issue I had to fix**: bundler resolved `rails 8.0.5.2` + `json 3.1.0`, and this stack's ActiveSupport passes `quirks_mode:` to `JSON.parse`/`JSON.generate`, which json 3.x removed — every JSON request 500'd. I pinned `rails` to exactly `8.0.2` and `json` to `2.9.1` (which still accepts that option), after which everything worked.\n\n**Other details**: `config/database.yml` has no hard-coded credentials (connection comes from `DATABASE_URL`, merged by Rails); production `force_ssl` disabled since the API serves plain HTTP; `start.sh` applies migrations with `db:prepare` (creates the DB on first run) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`, with a `SECRET_KEY_BASE` fallback so it boots even without `config/master.key`. README documents how to start the server.\n\nI tested every endpoint, all error paths, code-length boundaries, and confirmed clicks/data survive a full server restart. The test server is stopped and port 8000 is free for the grader's `sh start.sh`."
  }
